{"orgCode":"5170","name":"State Independent Living Council","agencyCode":"4000","agencyName":"Health and Human Services","description":"The State Independent Living Council's mission is to create policy and system change for independent living for persons with disabilities.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"positions":{"py":3,"cy":3,"by":3},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":716,"cy":755,"by":755}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/4000/5170","kind":"department","name":"State Independent Living Council","code":"5170","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"positions":{"py":3,"cy":3,"by":3},"byFundType":{},"children":[],"sources":[{"label":"ebudget.ca.gov API: orgProgram/5170","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/api/budget/e/2026-27/orgProgram/5170"},{"label":"Detailed Expenditures by Program (PDF)","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/GovernorsBudget/4000/5170.pdf"}],"extra":{"legalCitations":"DEPARTMENT AUTHORITY\n\nFederal-Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended by Title 29, United States Code Section 796d(a).\n\nState-Welfare and Institutions Code, Division 10, commencing with Section 19091."},"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/4000/5170/4250","kind":"program","name":"State Council Services","code":"4250","amounts":{"py":716,"cy":755,"by":755},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":716,"cy":755,"by":755}},"positions":{"py":3,"cy":3,"by":3},"description":"4250 - STATE COUNCIL SERVICES\n\nThe State Independent Living Council is responsible for developing a state plan for independent living and for monitoring, reviewing and evaluating the implementation of that plan. The Council also interacts with similar statewide councils to enhance the effectiveness of the network of centers that provide independent living services in California. The Council is required by the Federal Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, in order for the state to receive financial assistance for Independent Living Services and the Centers for Independent Living. The Council serves as an educational r